G1 is complete and verified. Summary of the step:

**What was implemented** (only two script files changed, per `git diff --stat`):

- `scripts/run/run_state.gd` — vote state on the open rope call: `_vote_yes: Dictionary[int, bool]`, `_vote_tally` getter (derived from the dict so count and record can't disagree), `record_yes_vote()`, `has_open_vote()`, `has_voted_yes()`, `vote_state()`, `reset_vote_state()`. Ownership comment updated to "Owned by run-economy (week 5)".
- `scripts/autoload/game_state.gd` — host-only `request_extract_vote(peer_id, yes)`: solo run ends immediately with `EXTRACT` (no tallying); co-op records yes votes and ends when every living player (`is_standing()` = not downed, not dead) has voted yes; a `no` cancels, resets and keeps the rope usable; a repeat yes from a peer whose vote is already recorded starts a fresh call (BRIEF Assumption 6 — rope.gd only forwards uses, so this is the one re-entry signal GameState receives); every change broadcasts `Events.rope_vote_updated(votes)` (signal already existed at `events.gd:62`, so no Events changes). `rope.gd` and `NetworkManager.request_vote_rope` untouched.

**Verification:**

- Full headless GUT suite: **1235/1235 tests pass**, 67 scripts — same counts as main (no test files touched, confirmed via `git status`/`git diff --stat`), so no regression and no count drift.
- `tools/smoke_two.sh`: **green, zero FAIL** — steps 1/2 (connect, spawn, movement both ways, leave), step 3 (spawn/hit/kill exactly once) and both floor-sync seed pairs all `ok`.
- Work sits on branch `feat/run-economy-W5-votes-deaths` (created off `main`), uncommitted and ready for the judge review alongside G2/G3/G4.

